{**
 * c-user-menu - whoever is signed in: a button carrying their name, and the
 * panel it opens with who they are, whatever the page offers them, and the ways
 * out.
 *
 * The panel is a native popover, opened by the button's popovertarget. That is
 * everything a menu has to do besides being drawn, and none of it is script of
 * this project's: a click outside it or Escape closes it, focus goes back to the
 * button, and the panel is drawn in the top layer - over the page and under
 * nothing, without a z-index. There is no token for one yet, and a panel that
 * needs none is no reason to invent it.
 *
 * The panel hangs under the button by CSS anchor positioning. The button is the
 * anchor and is named after the panel's id, so two menus on one page each find
 * their own button. Where a browser cannot anchor, assets/base.css puts the
 * panel in a fixed place under the banner instead, measured in theme tokens.
 *
 * Between who they are and the ways out sits whatever the caller puts in the
 * userMenuBody block - in the administration, the preference switch. The switch
 * is not drawn here, because the style guide shows this component on the very
 * page whose own switch is the specimen of c-preference-switcher, and two
 * switches on one page would be two controls for every answer.
 *
 * @param string $id the panel's id, which has to be unique on the page
 * @param string|null $testIdPrefix when given, every part carries a testid made
 *     from it: <prefix>-account-menu on the button, <prefix>-account-menu-panel
 *     on the panel, and <prefix>-identity, <prefix>-identity-email,
 *     <prefix>-public-link and <prefix>-sign-out inside it
 *}

{import 'button.latte'}

{define userMenu, string $id, string $name, string $email, string $signOutUrl, string $publicSiteUrl = '', ?string $testIdPrefix = null}
    {var array $testIds = $testIdPrefix === null ? [] : [
        'trigger' => $testIdPrefix . '-account-menu',
        'panel' => $testIdPrefix . '-account-menu-panel',
        'name' => $testIdPrefix . '-identity',
        'email' => $testIdPrefix . '-identity-email',
        'publicSite' => $testIdPrefix . '-public-link',
        'signOut' => $testIdPrefix . '-sign-out',
    ]}

    <div class="c-user-menu">
        {include button,
            label: $name,
            variant: 'quiet',
            icon: 'chevron-down',
            testId: $testIds['trigger'] ?? null,
            attributes: [
                'popovertarget' => $id,
                'style' => 'anchor-name: --' . $id,
            ]}

        <div
            id="{$id}"
            class="c-user-menu__panel"
            popover
            style="position-anchor: --{$id}"
            data-testid="{$testIds['panel'] ?? null}"
        >
            <p class="c-user-menu__who">
                <span class="c-user-menu__name" data-testid="{$testIds['name'] ?? null}">{$name}</span>
                <span class="c-user-menu__email" data-testid="{$testIds['email'] ?? null}">{$email}</span>
            </p>

            <div class="c-user-menu__body" n:ifcontent>{block userMenuBody}{/block}</div>

            <div class="c-user-menu__actions">
                {if $publicSiteUrl !== ''}
                    {include button,
                        label: 'Open the site',
                        href: $publicSiteUrl,
                        variant: 'quiet',
                        testId: $testIds['publicSite'] ?? null}
                {/if}

                {include button,
                    label: 'Sign out',
                    href: $signOutUrl,
                    variant: 'quiet',
                    icon: 'sign-out',
                    testId: $testIds['signOut'] ?? null}
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
{/define}
